<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the above assertion is incorrect because it doesn't correctly reflect the condition that elements at and after the insertion point should remain the same, except for the newly inserted element. The correct assertion should be:

<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

This ensures that all elements after the insertion point are shifted correctly and the elements at and after the insertion point retain their original values, except for the newly inserted element at the specified index.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the above assertion is incorrect because it suggests that elements starting from the insertion point are shifted to the left, which is the opposite of what actually happens. The correct assertion should reflect that elements at and after the insertion point are shifted to the right.

The correct assert statement should be:
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
--------------------
